        "Research from the European Union of the Deaf and national disability organisations consistently documents that the formal recognition of sign language in the Western Balkans has not translated to everyday accessibility infrastructure. Informal daily settings — the market, the café, the neighbourhood conversation — carry no legal obligation for captioning or signing and are therefore entirely inaccessible to deaf Serbians without a hearing companion. The slava — Serbia's most culturally specific annual family gathering — remains a noise-filled event that deaf family members observe rather than participate in. Captio AI captions Serbian speech in real time — including fast Belgrade colloquial Serbian and Ijekavian varieties — so the kafana, the market, and the family table are no longer conversations you have to sit outside of.",
