        "A 2025 PMC study on university adjustment among deaf and hard of hearing students found that communication barriers in lecture-based learning environments remain the primary driver of academic underperformance — independent of students' intellectual ability (PMC12505907, 2025). China has no formal national recognition of Chinese Sign Language as an official language. Certified interpreter provision in higher education is concentrated in cities and institutions with specialist programmes — not in the mainstream university lecture halls where most deaf students study.",
