        "The combination of Basque's linguistic uniqueness, the six-dialect landscape, the Basque-Spanish code-switching in clinical settings, and the absence of a dedicated Basque sign language tied to the deaf community's cultural experience creates an access problem unlike any other in Europe. A deaf Basque patient has no prior language from which to transfer lip-reading skills, limited interpreter access, and a healthcare system that communicates partly in a language (Spanish) that differs phonologically from Basque in every dimension. Captio AI captions Basque and Spanish in real time at any osasun-etxe or ospitale in the Basque Country and Navarre, so every patient receives their doctor's words directly.",
